{"words": [{"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "And who"}, {"text": "يَرْغَبُ", "translation": "will turn away"}, {"text": "عَن", "translation": "from"}, {"text": "مِّلَّةِ", "translation": "(the) religion"}, {"text": "إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ", "translation": "(of) Ibrahim"}, {"text": "إِلَّا", "translation": "except"}, {"text": "مَن", "translation": "who"}, {"text": "سَفِهَ", "translation": "fooled"}, {"text": "نَفْسَهُۥ ۚ", "translation": "himself"}, {"text": "وَلَقَدِ", "translation": "And indeed"}, {"text": "ٱصْطَفَيْنَـٰهُ", "translation": "We chose him"}, {"text": "فِى", "translation": "in"}, {"text": "ٱلدُّنْيَا ۖ", "translation": "the world"}, {"text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translation": "and indeed he"}, {"text": "فِى", "translation": "in"}, {"text": "ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ", "translation": "the Hereafter"}, {"text": "لَمِنَ", "translation": "surely (will be) among"}, {"text": "ٱلصَّـٰلِحِينَ", "translation": "the righteous"}], "sahih": "And who would be averse to the religion of Abraham except one who makes a fool of himself. And We had chosen him in this world, and indeed he, in the Hereafter, will be among the righteous."}